  "Scenes.Manor.LethiciteTunnel1.AtEndOfAdjacent": "At the end of this adjacent tunnel, you spot a faint pink light. You feel warm, just like you did when you first left Ingnam."
  "Scenes.Manor.LethiciteTunnel1.CrystalDestroyedTunnel": "With the crystal destroyed, this tunnel is now just as dark as the rest of the underground section."
  "Scenes.Manor.LethiciteTunnel2.CenterStands": "[pg]At the center of it stands an altar adorned with a massive, glowing lethicite crystal. Upon close examination, it appears it was made by joining smaller crystals together."
  "Scenes.Manor.LethiciteTunnel2.CenterStandsAgain": "[pg]At the center of it stands an altar, now covered in powerless shards of destroyed lethicite."
  "Scenes.Manor.LethiciteTunnel2.EnterChamberAtThe": "You enter a chamber at the end of the tunnel."
  "Scenes.Manor.LethiciteTunnel2.PerhapsBoreSomeType": " Perhaps it bore some type of connection to the necromancer you defeated?"
  "Scenes.Manor.LibraryRoom.NorthernBookshelfIs": "[pg]You notice the northern bookshelf is curiously built into the wall."
  "Scenes.Manor.LibraryRoom.WellStockedLibrary": "You're at a rather well stocked library. Bookshelves cover all four walls of the room, and they are tall enough to make you feel small by comparison."
  "Scenes.Manor.LibrarySecret.AlsoNoticeScatteredPages": "[pg]You also notice several scattered pages on the floor."
  "Scenes.Manor.LibrarySecret.InsideSecretRoom": "You're inside the secret room in the library. It is made of solid rock, contrasting the wooden finish of the rest of the manor. Carvings adorn the four walls of this room, depicting unknown tentacled creatures teaching humans the arts of magic. You hear a deep, slow beating sound, emanating from below your feet."
  "Scenes.Manor.LibrarySecret.NorthernWallThers": "[pg]On the northern wall, there's a circular, palm-sized slot. A lock, perhaps?"
  "Scenes.Manor.LibrarySecret.SeePassageToThe": "[pg]You see the passage to the underground chamber at the end of the room."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourt.CoughBloodCrippled": "[pg]You cough blood, crippled by massive pain. You barely have time to feel pain, however, as the jester lunges towards you. It barely misses once, slicing your skin, and you attempt to counter. Despite the clear opening, however, you miss your strike; the wizard hexed you as you attacked."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourt.LifeLeavesYou": "[pg]Your life leaves you moments afterwards. Your last sight is of a towering humanoid figure covered in a cloak, slowly shuffling towards you, hissing loudly."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourt.MoreDustMoreAshes": "[pg]<b>More dust. More ashes. More disappointment.</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourt.SlipAndFall": "[pg]You slip and fall. You turn to face the ceiling, but all you see is the grim grin of a skull, covered in a Jester's hat. He plunges his dagger into your chest, striking your heart."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourt.StaggerBackwards": "You stagger backwards from your injuries. You take a breath and try to retain your balance, but your attempt is foiled by a hefty mace crushing your chest and launching you into a wall."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.ApproachesYouSilent": "[pg]It approaches you, silent. Suddenly, its long, clawed hand darts out from underneath the cloak and grasps your head. Its sharp fingers slowly and agonizingly penetrate your skull."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.FallOverwhelmedBy": "You fall, overwhelmed by"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.FewMomentsOfIncredible": " After a few moments of incredible pain, the figure releases your head. It breathes deeply, disappointed, fingers dripping with blood. With its other hand, it reveals a long, bloodstained curved dagger. Your eyes widen as he shifts its grip to stab you, but there's nothing you can do. He swiftly plunges the dagger to your chest. The world blackens once more."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.LustRagingThrough": " the lust raging through you."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.MomentsIncrediblePain": " After a few moments of incredible pain, the figure releases your head. It lowers itself to face you directly, and you shiver in fear as he grasps your head with both of its clawed hands. [say: Ephraim,] he whispers in a damning tone to you. The word echoes inside your mind, louder and louder. You attempt to break free of his grasp, desperate. The echoes go louder, consuming your entire being. [say: Ephraim.] Overwhelmed, you black out."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.UndeadWizardTooMuch": " The undead wizard proved too much of a challenge to you, and you're at his mercy. It begins casting a long spell, somehow performing eldritch incantations despite its lack of lips or tongue. Unable to move, the spell hits you directly, and you go unconscious."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.WakeUpDazedBound": "[pg]You wake up, dazed and bound, on the cold stone ground of a large, dark chamber. A towering being completely covered in a red cloak slowly shuffles through tables, flipping pages, taking notes. It turns to you, its face nothing but a black nothingness, completely covered by its cloak. You feel a shiver run down your spine."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtier.YourWoundsWord": " your wounds."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtierEphraimd.EphraimYouAreEphraim": "[pg]Ephraim. You are Ephraim."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtierEphraimd.LookAtYourself": "[pg]You look at yourself from every angle, but everything appears to be normal. You feel odd, but shake the feeling away and leave your bedroom. You cannot waste time, after all. There are secrets about this manor to discover, about your long-forgotten ancestor and how he managed to find you, Ephraim."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtierEphraimd.WakeUpOnBed": "You wake up on your bed, in cold sweat. For a moment, you struggle to remember anything of what happened in the previous night, or anything about yourself at all. You get up and go towards your vanity, curious about your own look."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtierSkeletonized.AnotherLifeWasted": "[pg]<b>Another life wasted in the pursuit of glory and gold. </b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtierSkeletonized.BriefStateOf": "[pg]You enter a brief state of panic, but it doesn't last for long. Suddenly, all ability to think is removed from your being. One thought remains, all-consuming, absolute: \"Protect Ephraim\". You accept it, your decaying corpse rising up and moving to patrol the manor. This is the end of your life, and the rest of eternity."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCourtierSkeletonized.RegainSensesAgain": "You regain your senses once again, but you feel cold, numb. You attempt to recall where you were, but you cannot remember. You attempt to recall what you were doing, but you cannot remember. Finally, a deciding question hits your mind. Who are you? You cannot remember."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.BeforeYouCanEnjoy": ". Before you can properly enjoy your orgasm, another wave hits you, making you scream and drool with the insane amount of pleasure you're receiving."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.DespiteMindCompletely": "[pg]Despite having your mind be completely fucked by the crystal, somehow, you desire more. Somehow, you feel like you have a dozen pair of hefty breasts, several bloated cocks, tens of pussies aching to be filled. Your mind is awash with hundreds of sexual encounters, and in each of those, you beg for more."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.EjaculatingThickStrands": ", ejaculating thick strands of semen onto the air"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.FallDownTooAroused": "You fall down, too aroused to continue fighting."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.ImmediatelyAttemptMasturbate": "[pg]You immediately attempt to masturbate, but the lethicite crystal pulses again. When it hits you, you begin convulsing in spontaneous orgasm"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.SquirtingUncannyAmounts": ", squirting uncanny amounts of pussy juice onto the ground"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal.StandUpTrembling": "[pg]You stand up, trembling with desire, and charge towards the lethicite crystal, intent on absorbing as much of its corrupted pleasure as possible. Another pulse hits you, and you pass out."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal2.HissesStandsUpAttaches": "[pg]He hisses, stands up, and attaches the small crystal to the altar."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal2.LeavesShortlyAfterwards": "[pg]He leaves. Shortly afterwards, a group of armed skeletons enter the chamber. You open your demonic eyes, disappointed that none of them have genitals for you to fuck. They execute you mercilessly as you begin masturbating, too drunk on pleasure to care about your own life."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToCrystal2.WhileUnconsciousTowering": "While you're unconscious, a towering figure shuffles into the chamber. It approaches you and kneels. It extends a fleshy, clawed hand and plucks something out of the puddle created by your mad rush of pleasure. A lethicite crystal."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToGeneral.CollapseTooWeak": "You collapse, too weak to continue fighting. You couldn't have expected such ghoulish horrors so early into this journey! Your only hope is that the monstrosity that defeated you deigns you too weak to be a threat."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToGeneral.DeadMoreBlood": "[pg]<b>You are dead. More blood soaks the soil, feeding the evil therein.</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToGeneral.ShamblesTowardsYou": "[pg]It shambles towards you, dragging its mace on the ground. When it reaches you, it holds it aloft. It swiftly brings it down, crushing your entire body with the heft of the massive weapon."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJester.FallOverwhelmedBy": "You fall, overwhelmed by"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJester.JesterJumpsOnTable": "The shifty jester jumps on top of the dining table as you groan, twitching and jingling while watching your precarious situation. You look down to the ground for a moment, and when you look up, the skeleton is gone. You exhale in desperation as you search for him, but you soon discover his location, as a sharp blade rests against your neck."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJester.LustRagingThrough": " the lust raging through you."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJester.UncannyStrengthSlices": " With uncanny strength, he slices your throat open. Blood surging through your mouth is the last thing you feel before you faint, barely capable of comprehending your death."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJester.YourWoundsWord": " your wounds."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.AttemptMoveAgain": "[pg]You attempt move again, growing increasingly desperate. Your heart sinks and you stand breathless when something else stumbles into view, lit by the torches on the walls; <b>your own body</b>. You look down, slowly, panicked, and find you're just a disembodied head, placed on a ritual circle."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.BrieflyOverwhelmHorror": "[pg]You briefly overwhelm your horror and do your best to make your body attack the cloaked figure, but he immediately grasps your head, causing all thoughts of rebellion to fade. He digs his claws deep into your skull, and your eyes widen in panic as you feel your memories and self burn away, victim of eldritch magic."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.HissesForMoment": "[pg]It hisses for a moment, and then begins carving something on your forehead. You scream in pain as he tears your [skin] and attempt to stop him, but your body doesn't obey any of your commands."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.NearlyBlindedBy": "You are nearly blinded by the pain by the time the figure stops its carving. He then chants some words you do not recognize. Shortly afterwards, you feel your body again, as if it was numbed before. You move your body, but oddly, you remain in the same place."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.SomethingMovesInto": "[pg]Something moves into your vision. A towering entity completely covered in a red cloak shuffles towards you. It lowers itself as it lifts one of its fingers towards your forehead; a long, dried and clawed appendage."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.SoonTurnedIntoA": "[pg]Soon, you're turned into a husk. Only one thought races through your ravaged mind: \"Gather more souls\". You command your body to reattach yourself to it, and, with your master's blessing, move out of the manor and into Mareth, to gather as many souls as possible, for whatever purposes he desires."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToJesterDullahand.WakeUpScreaming": "You wake up, screaming. You immediately notice you're no longer in the dining room. You attempt to survey your dark, faintly lit surroundings, but you find it curiously hard to move or feel your body at all."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNamelessHorror.FallDefeatedByHorror": "You fall, defeated by the horrifying abomination. It quickly bends space itself to stand next to you."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNamelessHorror.NoHope": "<b>There can be no hope in this hell. No hope at all.</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNamelessHorror.StareUponItsFace": "[pg]You stare upon its face-stalk, cowering in terror. The Thing shrieks, points at you, and you are instantly disassembled."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNecro.FallOverwhelmedByNecromancer": "You fall, overwhelmed by the Necromancer's minions. You look around, spotting the piles of corpses and skeletons that provide this place with a grim decoration. You shut your eyes, knowing that you'll soon be part of them."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNecro.FewMomentsOfIncredible": " After a few moments of incredible pain, the figure releases your head. It breathes deeply, disappointed, fingers dripping with blood. With its other hand, it reveals a long, bloodstained curved dagger. Your eyes widen as he shifts its grip to stab you, but there's nothing you can do. He swiftly plunges the dagger to your chest. The world blackens once more."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNecro.MomentsIncrediblePain": " After a few moments of incredible pain, the figure releases your head. It lowers itself to face you directly, and you shiver in fear as he grasps your head with both of its clawed hands. [say: Ephraim,] he whispers in a damning tone to you. The word echoes inside your mind, louder and louder. You attempt to break free of his grasp, desperate. The echoes go louder, consuming your entire being. [say: Ephraim.] Overwhelmed, you black out."
  "Scenes.Manor.LoseToNecro.NecromancerApproaches": "[pg]The necromancer approaches you, silent. Suddenly, its long, clawed hand darts out from underneath the cloak and grasps your head. Its sharp fingers slowly and agonizingly penetrate your skull."
  "Scenes.Manor.MainHall.StandAtSpaciousMain": "You stand at the spacious main hall of the manor. Cobwebs cover most of the corners of the manor, and the smell of mold and rotten wood is ubiquitous. The mansion almost appears alive, as it constantly creaks under its own weight. The middling light that invades this room lights up several specks of dust, further confirming the state of disrepair of this manor."
  "Scenes.Manor.MainHall.TatteredRegalRug": "[pg]A tattered, regal rug adorns the center of the room, crowned by a broken chandelier that must have crashed onto the floor years ago. Most windows are covered by velvet drapes, most of them broken beyond repair. To your right, you see a corridor leading towards a set of stairs. In front of you, there's a set of wide wooden doors, leading to what you believe is a dining room. To your left, there's an arch leading to a library."
  "Scenes.Manor.NorthBookshelf.ApproachOddBookshelf": "You approach the odd bookshelf. Most books are worn beyond all recognition, but you can still make out the names of a few of them from their spines."
  "Scenes.Manor.NorthBookshelf.CodespellWord": "<b>{0}</b>[pg]"
  "Scenes.Manor.NorthBookshelf.PlacingLastBookBack": "Upon placing the last book back into the shelf, you hear a click, and a small section of the bookshelf moves inside the wall with a deep rumbling noise. After sliding back a few inches, it moves to the side, <b>revealing a hidden passage!</b>[pg]"
  "Scenes.Manor.OpenStairs.PeerIntoGap": "[pg]You peer into the gap created by the sliding wall as it lowers, revealing a dark tunnel, descending into the underground. Unblocked by the wall, the beating sound intensifies, making you breathe deeply in anxiety. Something tells you that <b>you should be well prepared before heading forward.</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.OpenStairs.PressTheTalisman": "You carefully press the talisman you've found into the slot. The shapes match perfectly, and as you finish the insertion you hear a satisfying, deep 'click' noise. A few moments later several sounds of mechanical devices in action emanate from the wall. Then, it begins slowly sliding down, slightly shaking as stone scrapes against stone. The talisman is ejected from the slot, and you quickly pick it back up."
  "Scenes.Manor.ReadStudyBooks.ReadSomePages": "You read some pages of a few of the books on the shelves, the ones not too worn down to be read. They range from simple, dull accounting of servants, finances and products to assorted blasé romances. Boring, but hardly terrifying."
  "Scenes.Manor.RoomCourtyard.ApproachRottenDoor": "You approach the rotten door to the manor, preparing to tear it down with whatever you have on hand. The worn wood barely manages to stay connected to the hinges, so you know it won't be much work."
  "Scenes.Manor.RoomCourtyard.CrowsGatherDeadTrees": "[pg]Crows gather around the dead trees that surround the courtyard, a final touch to the brooding feel of the ruined place."
  "Scenes.Manor.RoomCourtyard.DoorViolentlyDestroyed": "[pg]Suddenly, the door is violently destroyed from within, the shards flying towards you! You manage to dodge in time, but your stomach sinks when you spot the being that destroyed it; an enormous, 8-foot tall armored skeleton, wielding a gigantic mace!"
  "Scenes.Manor.RoomCourtyard.EnterCombatStance": "[pg]You enter a combat stance. You're fighting a <b>Bone Guardian!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.RoomCourtyard.StandAtDecrepitCourtyard": "You stand at the decrepit courtyard of the old Manor. The vegetation has overtaken much of the stone walkways. A fountain and a statue that once depicted a member of the manor's family lies ruined beyond recognition. Several tents lie destroyed, blood staining some of the worn fabric, as if a great fight took place here."
  "Scenes.Manor.RoomCourtyard.TremorCausesBrief": "[pg]A tremor causes you to briefly lose your balance while moving forward. You continue to approach, wary of any nearby threat. As you close your distance to the door, the tremors get stronger, causing the nearby crows to flee. You ready yourself."
  "Scenes.Manor.Stairs0.AtBaseOf": "You're at the base of the stairs leading up to the second floor."
  "Scenes.Manor.Stairs1.SecondFloor": "You're in the second floor of the forgotten manor. It is in as much of a state of disrepair as the first floor. Several portraits of humans adorn the walls through the corridor, some resting on the ground. You assume them to be the house's ancestry, but it is hard to tell; the paintings have been defaced, \"Ephraim\" carved into all of them. Most of the rooms are inaccessible, the roof having collapsed over them."
  "Scenes.Manor.Stairs2.FeelOddApproaching": "You feel odd as you approach the stairs. It is hard to describe, but you feel a clutching sense of impeding doom. The walls of the corridor close in, space itself bending to give you vertigo. The many shadows appear to grow, nightmarish creatures taking form from within, approaching you. The feeling grows steadily as you get closer to the stairs. When you're at the edge, you feel absolutely terrified."
  "Scenes.Manor.Stairs2.SecondFloor": "You're in the second floor of the forgotten manor. It is in as much of a state of disrepair as the first floor. Several portraits of humans adorn the walls through the corridor, some resting on the ground. You assume them to be the house's ancestry, but it is hard to tell; the paintings have been defaced, \"Ephraim\" carved into all of them. Most of the rooms are inaccessible, the roof having collapsed over them."
  "Scenes.Manor.Stairs3.SecondFloor": "You're in the second floor of the forgotten manor. It is in as much of a state of disrepair as the first floor. Several portraits of humans adorn the walls through the corridor, some resting on the ground. You assume them to be the house's ancestry, but it is hard to tell; the paintings have been defaced, \"Ephraim\" carved into all of them. Most of the rooms are inaccessible, the roof having collapsed over them."
  "Scenes.Manor.StairsStart.CorridorTo": "You're at a corridor to the right of the main hall. Although it probably would have gone on for the entire west section of the manor, it is caved in, impassable. Under the debris, you can see a skeleton clutching a bloodied pickaxe, signaling that this collapse wasn't caused by natural causes."
  "Scenes.Manor.StairsStart.DespiteBlockage": "[pg]Despite the blockage, you can still go up the wide stairs that lead to the second floor of the manor."
  "Scenes.Manor.Study.AlthoughManyBooks": "[pg]Although many of the books and documents have aged beyond reading, there is a set of curiously pristine pages on a desk, presumably torn from some journal."
  "Scenes.Manor.Study.SomeKindOf": "You're at some kind of private study. Tattered journals and books adorn the many bookcases and desks. There's a window to the yard behind the manor, allowing some of the outside light to light up the cobwebs and the dust within. The yard also stands overgrown, and there are multiple headstones in the distance; the deceased ancestry of this house."
  "Scenes.Manor.TablePages.NewCodexEntryManor": "[pg]<b>New codex entry unlocked: Manor Journal!</b>[pg]"
  "Scenes.Manor.TakeBooks.CollectTomesGently": "[pg]You collect the tomes as gently as possible, thankfully managing to get them into your [inv] without damaging any. The weight [if (str < 40) {is a bit much, but you'll make do|doesn't bother you [if (str < 70) {much|at all}]}] as you turn back to face the rest of the aging estate."
  "Scenes.Manor.TakeBooks.NotSureExactlyWhere": "You're not sure exactly where they'll end up, but you know for a fact that these books aren't doing anyone any good just rotting on these shelves."
  "Scenes.Manor.TakeBooks.OldManorBooks": "[pg][b:Key item gained: Old Manor Books!]"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.AnotherTestOfConstitution": "Another test of your constitution, of your willpower. Your life has dealt you harsh lessons, but it affects you not. Your mind is ironclad, your hope unyielding! You are <b>Stalwart!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.AreYouDead": "Are you dead? Can you even remember who you are? Three stars, two moons, one horse. You are <b>Irrational!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.FacedWithTerrors": "Faced with these terrors, you reach the aphotic conclusion that was long due to you. You will not survive this. The wind whispers of your failure, and you heed its call, trembling. You are <b>Fearful!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.MomentOfUtterTerror": "In this moment of utter terror and hardship, your mind clears up. Perfect, unyielding clarity. You have an objective, and success relies only on your practiced skills. Success, then, will be achieved. You are <b>Focused!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.RememberThePain": "You remember the pain from all the blows and attacks you've suffered. They have forged you into a stronger person, a better person! You need more of it! You are <b>Masochistic!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.StandOverAllChallenges": "You will stand over all challenges and survive! You feel energized, confident in yourself. You are <b>Vigorous!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.VastTerrorsMotivate": "Such vast terrors only motivate you to fight better, harder. You will rise up, and tear victory from the maws of doom, no matter the cost! You are <b>Powerful!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TestResolve.WeakApatheticVictory": "You feel... weak. Apathetic. A victory here, for what purpose? Evil is timeless, unending. You will lose eventually. You are <b>Depressed!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TheChamber.ApproachMassiveChamber": "You approach a massive chamber, much better lit than the tunnel before you. Corpses and skeletons are strewn in great mounds, with piles of books, alchemy tables, cages and ritual circles spread around the grim room."
  "Scenes.Manor.TheChamber.FigureLiftsArm": "[pg]The figure lifts its arm, revealing a scroll grasped by a hideous, fleshy and clawed hand. It shrieks, and before your eyes, several bones in one of the nearby piles assembles itself, becoming another skeleton! You're fighting a <b>Necromancer!</b>"
  "Scenes.Manor.TheChamber.LaidOverTorchAltar": " Laid over a torch - shaped altar is a towering humanoid being, completely covered in a red cloak."
  "Scenes.Manor.TheChamber.NearbyTableYouSee": "[pg]On a nearby table, you see a few scattered pages."
  "Scenes.Manor.TheChamber.SeeDarkCrystal": "[pg]You see a dark crystal on the ground, the remains of the dagger the Necromancer used to kill himself."
  "Scenes.Manor.TheChamber.TurnsToFaceYou": "[pg]It turns to face you. [say: The Flesh turns against itself. Like a tumor. You come here, to undo what I have created, to attempt to perpetuate the illusion that binds all living beings in this universe, foolishly seeking to undo \"evil\". I know better. And I will show you.]"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels1.AirFeelsCool": "[pg]The air feels cool on your [skin], and you notice the faint smell of chemicals emanating from deeper within the corridor.{0}"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels1.GoDownCarefully": "You go down carefully, the darkness gradually overwhelming your sight. Before long you reach the end of the stairs and attempt to discern your environment as best you can."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels1.MoveThroughGateway": "You move through the unlocked gateway to the manor's depths. Despite the necromancer's demise, you can't help but still feel a sense of dread as you go down the shadow-cloaked stairs."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels1.ReachEndOfThe": "You reach the end of the corridor and see the stairs leading back to the manor's library. You feel compelled to climb them, as if you had to surface from deep underwater to inhale fresh air."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels1.StandAtBeginning": "[pg]You stand at the beginning of a long corridor, its length only barely perceptible due to the illumination provided by a series of dim torches spread throughout the stone walls. The stonework is noticeably high quality, and the same applies to the floor. Whatever this place is, it was made with care, and built to last."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.IntuitionLeadsYou": "[pg]Your intuition leads you to check your back, and, as expected, there stands the undead jester, twitching with one of his daggers on hand. The <b>Bone Jester</b> is also back!"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.IntuitionLeadsYouAgain": "[pg]Your intuition leads you to check your back, and, to your surprise, there stands another skeleton, dressed with a jester's garb and twitching unnaturally while in a combat position, dual wielding daggers. You're fighting a <b>Bone Jester</b>!"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.MoveForwardFewFeet": "[pg]You move forward a few feet, and immediately jump and roll to the side as a familiar mace crushes the stone floor! The <b>Bone Guardian</b> has somehow come back to life, and is blocking your path!"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.MoveThroughTunnelSlowly": "You move through the tunnel slowly, inching forward, aided by the dim torches that adorn the walls."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.NoWayAroundIt": "[pg]No way around it. You'll have to fight all three of the manor's guardians at once!"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.OfEldritchChanting": "[pg]Of eldritch chanting."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.OfRattlingBones": "[pg]Of rattling bones."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.PrepareToFight": "[pg]You prepare to fight, but you're thrown off focus when you see a smaller figure appear next to the armored skeleton. The <b>Bone Sorcerer</b> has also returned to life!"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.SeeDarkCurvedDagger": "[pg]You see a dark, curved dagger laying on the floor. Perhaps it was left by the undead jester?"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels2.SuddenlyHearSound": "[pg]Suddenly, you hear the sound of clanking armor."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels3.DespiteNecromancerDefeat": "Despite the Necromancer's defeat, you still feel unease when traversing these tunnels."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels3.WantedToFreeMyself": "[say: I did many things I regret. I would, however, do them again. This world is an illusion. The constant nightmares I had when I first visited this manor were at first a sign of madness, but later, a glimpse of truth.[pg]I wanted to free myself. To be granted the cosmic sight that reveals the true nature of the Universe. No human had the lifespan or the intuition required to properly tear open the gates to the Abyss. The only option, then, was to become more than human.]"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels4.DespiteNecromancerDefeat": "Despite the Necromancer's defeat, you still feel unease when traversing these tunnels."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels4.WorkersEvelyn": "[say: The Thing I have become is perhaps a fitting resolution to my folly, my curiosity turned obsession. I cannot tell what the point of no return was. In the beginning, I was just a young man, eager to uncover secrets of my ancestry. In the end, many innocents paid for my unspeakable transgressions of nature.[pg]The workers, Evelyn, and the uncountable amount of souls she's harvested over the years.]"
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels5.DespiteNecromancerDefeat": "Despite the Necromancer's defeat, you still feel unease when traversing these tunnels."
  "Scenes.Manor.Tunnels5.RegardlessOfEthics": "[say: Regardless of the ethics of my plans, however, it is still imperative that I succeed. Move forward if you must. But know that you'll be feeding my ambitions by doing so, and further extending my objectives.]"
  "Scenes.Manor.UseCrystal.HardToTearAway": "[pg]You find it hard to tear your gaze from the infinite void beyond the crystal. You're somehow reminded of the manor, and of the blasphemous chamber underneath it, and the profane rituals performed at the dead of night."
  "Scenes.Manor.UseCrystal.LiftCrystalAgain": "You lift the crystal and peer through it, staring at its many blinking dots, which shine like stars in the night sky. It is certainly beautiful in its own way, but it doesn't mean much."
  "Scenes.Manor.UseCrystal.LiftCrystalAndPeer": "You lift the crystal and peer through it, staring at its many blinking dots, which shine like stars. It should be impossible, but the area inside the crystal is bigger than its volume. Infinitely bigger."
  "Scenes.Manor.UseCrystal.RoomTurnsPitchBlack": "[pg]The already dark room turns pitch black, and the crystal fades from your grasp. The window to infinity, however, does not. It expands, slowly swallowing the entire room. You panic and attempt to run, but it is too late! You're enveloped by the cosmic lattice, overwhelmed by eternity."
  "Scenes.Manor.UseCrystal.WidenYourEyes": "[pg]You widen your eyes gradually as the truth dawns upon you. This crystal is a window! To another dimension, to another world or to this reality, you're unsure. But there's no doubt in your mind. You try to pry your eyes away from it, but you cannot. You're completely dazed by the glimpse of infinity."
}
